From 5ada1a9231533e97e5d0562c3735d3d6041e26be Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: NeoTech <andreas@roughedge.se>
Date: Sun, 8 Nov 2026 00:51:35 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] feat(motion): the scallop law's reach ceiling - a stepover at
 the ball diameter is refused

The ridge flank law reads a cusp only to 4*tol past the ball (s ~ 2.9 on
an r3 ball), and the 3D finish door accepted any positive stepover, so a
spacing past that verified silent on scallop. The generator now refuses,
by name, a stated stepover or steep stepover at or past the ball diameter
(past s = 2r the cusp formula h = r - sqrt(r^2 - (s/2)^2) describes uncut
ground, not a cusp) and a tolerance at or past r/2 (where the auto law
sqrt(8 r tol) reaches 2r). The scan's reach stays band + 3*tol with its
validity range documented: a 2r far tier was built and measured, and it
convicted the cone apex, box walls and dome crown (11 verdict-lane tests),
so it waits on a crown/corner exclusion (RECOMMENDED "#37").

Pinned by scallop_ceiling (at / just under / past the diameter and r/2,
degenerate radius and tolerance); the authored-ladder test moves from
steep_stepover 8 to 5 on the 6 mm ball.

Fixes #37

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
